> Er, do you mean blindness? Also, this makes the (currently justified)
> assumption that all gaze attacks are "harmful sensation" attacks; I
> think there are some mythological creatures that can kill you with
> their gaze even if you're not aware of it personally (which would be a
> better match to the term "gaze attack"). Also, what happens if the
> *monster* is blind? Since all of NetHack's current gazes appear to rely
> on your eyes meeting theirs, I'm inclined to say that this should stop
